  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "slug-suffix-rule-is-bidirectional",
      "finding": "The country suffix is required for ambiguous city names and breaks unambiguous ones. Hiroshima, Kanazawa, Nara, Krakow and Cusco all 404 bare and resolve with a country suffix; Aomori, Cartagena and Phuket resolve bare and 404 with the suffix. Slug resolution must therefore try both forms rather than applying one rule, and the source's error page names the correct target in both directions, which makes it automatable."
    },
    {
      "id": "rate-limit-observed",
      "finding": "The source returned HTTP 429 after roughly 40 page fetches in quick succession. A full 121-city refresh must be paced or checkpointed rather than issued as one burst. This is an operational constraint on the refresh design, not on feasibility."
    },
    {
      "id": "long-tail-attrition-quantified",
      "finding": "Of the drawn low-band destinations, five had no source page at all (Lombok, Luang Prabang, Hoi An, Kampot, Mui Ne) and three more were rejected for zero or near-zero contributors (Pai, Aomori, Cusco). Level-1 coverage is effectively complete for cities and sparse for village and island destinations, which is the same boundary the earlier reconnaissance found and the reason the cascade exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "thin-source-cities-retained-not-dropped",
      "finding": "Seven retained cities carry a low contributor count. Rather than applying a hard floor, they are flagged so the fit can be run with and without them. Whether thin sources move the coefficients is an empirical question the sample can now answer, and a hard cut would discard exactly the low-band cities the mcmeal relationship most needs."
    }
  ]
}
